#. Plugin Name of the plugin
#: baukasten-2fa.php
msgid "Baukasten Addon: Two-Factor Approval"
msgstr ""

#. Plugin URI of the plugin
#: baukasten-2fa.php
msgid "https://github.com/trstnbde/baukasten"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: baukasten-2fa.php
msgid "Adds a two-factor method that asks a second, already signed-in browser session to approve the login from the WordPress admin bar."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: baukasten-2fa.php
msgid "Torsten B."
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: baukasten-2fa.php
msgid "https://github.com/trstnbde"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:17
msgid "Adds a second factor that asks another browser instead of asking for a code: when someone signs in, every other session that is already signed in shows a confirmation in its admin bar."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:22
msgid "The Two Factor plugin is not active, so this method is not being offered to anyone."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:26
msgid "The Two Factor settings list which methods this site allows, and this one is not on it. Until it is, nobody can select it on their profile."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:29
#: includes/class-notices.php:88
msgid "Allow this method site-wide"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:35
msgid "Timing"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:45
msgid "How long a request waits"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:58
#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:83
#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:114
msgid "seconds"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:61
msgid "The other browser learns about the request through the WordPress heartbeat, which ticks about once a minute and slows down further in a tab that has been idle for a while. Allow for up to a minute before the confirmation appears — if people report that requests expire before they see them, raise this."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:71
msgid "Check every"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:85
msgid "Only while a request is actually open. The rest of the time nothing is polled beyond the heartbeat that runs anyway."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:90
msgid "Requests per user"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:101
msgid "requests"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:104
msgid "within"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:117
msgid "Stops repeated sign-in attempts from filling somebody's admin bar with confirmations."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:124
msgid "What the prompt shows"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:129
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:138
msgid "Show where the sign-in came from"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:142
msgid "A shortened address and a rough browser name, so the question \"was that you?\" can actually be answered. The full address and the full browser string are never stored."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:151
msgid "Idle tabs"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:160
msgid "Keep checking in an idle wp-admin tab"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:164
msgid "WordPress stops its heartbeat in a tab nobody has touched for a few minutes — which is usually exactly the tab that should be showing the confirmation. This keeps it going in the dashboard only, never on the public site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:174
msgid "Keep records for"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:186
msgid "hours"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:188
msgid "Answered and expired requests are deleted after this. They are kept at all only so repeated requests can be counted."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:198
msgid "Turning it on"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to the current user's profile screen.
#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:204
#, php-format
msgid "Each person switches this on for themselves under Two-Factor Options on their %s."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:208
msgid "profile"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings-tab.php:216
msgid "Worth keeping a second method switched on as well. If no other session is open when a request goes out, this one simply waits until it expires — the sign-in page then offers the other methods."
msgstr ""

